es explicit disclosure\\n161: and does not establish an independent NL audit.\\n162: \\n163: ## A0. Freeze and disclose\\n164: \\n165: Read the original problem and independently check `spec.json`: target,\\n166: quantifiers, all H roots, parameter ranges, definitions, representatives,\\n167: normalization, endpoint conventions, and one-target scope. No H may originate\\n168: from the proof writer's desired conclusion. Audit target semantics, not just\\n169: hash equality. Record reviewer/carrier, shared context, read artifacts, and\\n170: whether any reference solution was seen. Read the canonical graph, not only\\n171: its generated Markdown. Bind the receipt to spec/graph hashes.\\n172: Generate the exhaustive global index with\\n173: `python3 nl0/scripts/nl0.py overview nl0.json --spec spec.json --out global-overview.json`.\\n174: It preserves every actual H (including unused or late-appended H), full global\\n175: statements/definitions and dependency edges with canonical pointers and hashes.\\n176: Read this inventory before claiming a node/condition is absent; a partial line\\n177: page cannot establish absence. The index supplies no verdict and does not\\n178: replace inspection of the relevant canonical proof and primary-source content.\\n179: The clean test adapter uses this same core generator, not a separate inventory\\n180: or mathematical standard.\\n181: Original-problem/source fidelity and local proof validity are separate tasks.\\n182: The original text may be read for target and citation checks; it may not fill\\n183: missing content during per-R packet-only replay. Record the actual boundary.\\n184: Check that original conditions really are H nodes, rather than predicates\\n185: hidden in a globally visible parameter type. A prime/nonzero condition,\\n186: characteristic constraint, range or equation must not become available to an\\n187: R with empty inputs through that encoding. Matching the full closed theorem\\n188: alone does not establish correct per-R H availability.\\n189: \\n190: ## A1. Definitions and notation\\n191: \\n192: For each D record a verdict with a concrete explanation. Check unique meaning,\\n193: type/domain, global versus local binding, definition dependencies, construction\\n194: or existence prerequisites, and applicability at every use. A guarded symbol\\n195: must not supply its own prerequisite. Record arbitrary choices, parameter\\n196: dependencies, and equivalence to the original definition. No project theorem\\n197: may hide as a definition, record field, predicate, or typeclass assumption.\\n198: \\n199: Reverse-check every actual mathematical object occurrence against a legitimate\\n200: declaration. Inspect local introduction position, first use, type/domain,\\n201: basis and end scope. Input-bound variables are not free locals; witnesses need\\n202: proved existence. Merely checking registered symbol names misses unregistered\\n203: ones. Definitions cannot smuggle properties or extra ancestor statements.\\n204: \\n205: ## A2. Sources\\n206: \\n207: For each M read the pinned official file and a successful full Lean signature\\n208: probe, not merely a `#check` name or a search result. Confirm declaration kind,\\n209: restatement, all implicit/typeclass assumptions, source hashes and commit,\\n210: relevant axioms, and suitability of scalar fields/domains. Library definitions\\n211: are not theorems. These source checks belong to global review; each using R's\\n212: packet review inspects its actual application mappings and premise discharge.\\n213: \\n214: For each E execute all nine requirements in\\n215: [external-theorem review](external-theorems.md). Give separate evidence-bound\\n216: verdicts for document identity, occurrence of the actual result, faithful\\n217: statement, complete surrounding context, and version/source eligibility.\\n218: Record every actual application separately in its using R, including repeated\\n219: uses of E in one R; packet review checks those applications. Global review\\n220: checks the source identity and statement. Source existence, exact citation and valid application are separate\\n221: obligations. Substantive transformations require an N proof. Do not infer any\\n222: of these verdicts from a historical audit or a successful Lean build.\\n223: \\n224: ### Paywalled or inaccessible primary text\\n225: \\n226: Search public sources using the title, DOI and authors: Google, arXiv,\\n227: author manuscripts, institutional repositories and accessible publisher text.\\n228: Use actual source readback, not a search snippet. A different readable version\\n229: must be identified honestly and checked against its own statement and context.\\n230: A page requiring JavaScript, login, payment or human verification is an access\\n231: limitation; do not bypass it or treat the page as the theorem text.\\n232: \\n233: When the primary text remains inaccessible, follow the exact\\n234: [conditional-source contract](conditional-sources.md). A complete statement\\n235: actually quoted in a supplied secondary source may remain an explicit E\\n236: assumption with a bound access-failure record. Keep its source review and\\n237: unperformed citation checks UNVERIFIED. Every mathematical/application check\\n238: must still be performed, and actual mismatches remain FAIL. Same-author closing\\n239: readiness may disclose this source uncertainty separately from mathematical\\n240: or inventory defects; it is not a verified-source claim.\\n241: \\n242: Continue the remaining work under that declared condition. A conditional A\\n243: receipt can enter Lean work, but cannot be labeled DRAFT-AUDIT-PASSED. If local\\n244: proofs, assembly and independent endpoint review succeed, the final status is\\n245: WORKFLOW-CONDITIONAL with warn.json/warn.md and an explicit user-facing list of\\n246: unchecked sources. A missing complete statement remains a missing input; do not\\n247: invent it. Full acceptance requires actual primary-source verification.\\n248: \\n249: ## A3. Structure\\n250: \"}"}}

